{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789303357,"nonce":"PKeaeH66bMTY/ry35gLzMaZ0qUA=","title":"A compiled frame's stack trace names the entry line and loses inlined callees","message":"Reproducer: a function `boom()` that throws at Kaboom.hx:3, called from\n`main` at Kaboom.hx:18 with `--mode jit`. The uncaught-exception trace\nprinted `Kaboom.main(Kaboom.hx:14)` (main's entry line, not the call site)\nand a bogus `Fun_385(.../Date.hx:0)` frame; there was no `boom` frame at\nall. `--mode interp` and `--mode hybrid` printed `Kaboom.boom(Kaboom.hx:3)`\nthen `Kaboom.main(Kaboom.hx:18)`.\n\nThree separate causes:\n\n1. Cranelift bodies carried one source position: the function's entry line\n   (`pack_position`), so every pc in a body mapped to the same line.\n2. The inliner copied a callee's body into the caller and dropped its\n   positions, so a throw inside inlined code was attributed to the caller\n   (`main` for `boom`), and the callee never appeared. The interpreter's\n   optimized-body debug table had the same gap: `optimized_debug` realigned\n   by LCS against the raw opcode table and lost inlined regions.\n3. On Linux x86-64, glibc `backtrace()` stops at the first JIT frame (no\n   `.eh_frame` for Cranelift code), so the walk from the C boundary\n   (`ash_throw_stack_boundary`) had only the caller chain via rbp and lost\n   the innermost compiled pc.\n\nFix: `air::v2` carries `Instr::Pos { file, line, site }` markers by default\n(`ASH_TRACE_LINES=0` turns them off); the inliner records an `InlineSite`\nper call and retags copied markers, so a pc expands to a chain of frames\ninnermost-first (`positions::for_each_frame`). The Cranelift tier turns\neach marker into a `SourceLoc` (sentinel base loc so the relative encoding\ncannot wrap) and the backend records `SourceRun`s per body, including OSR\nentries. The walker keeps `Prepared::positions`/`inline_sites` (markers\nstripped from its own IR copy so the dispatch loop does not pay for them)\nand expands frames through `frames_at`. Linux combines `backtrace()` for\nthe innermost pc with the rbp chain for the callers.\n\nFixture: crates/ash/test/tests/TestTraceInlined.hx (callStack,\nexceptionStack, uncaught throw across a three-deep inlined chain); all four\nengine arms print identical stdout+stderr on macOS and Linux.\n\nStill open, split out: 8aa6c55 (LLVM bodies have no source map, so a\nre-tiered function in `--mode hybrid` reports its entry line again).","files":null}]}